invariant: INV-17
file: sha512.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha512-avx2
reason: sha512_hw.c's copy of sha512.c's first arm, which an x86-64 session
  with CH_CPU_AVX2 runs, calls sha512_avx2_compress_blocks and never wipes
  the stack below the call, so the kernel's dead frame keeps the last
  sixteen schedule words of the last block, each plus its round constant.
  Under HMAC-SHA-384 the first block is the key, and those words give
  back the block. Every digest is still right, so no vector sees it, and
  the arm under sha512.c's own names still wipes. bin/sha2_equiv_test
  paints the stack, makes each kind of call on sha512_hw.c, and requires
  no word the call computed in the bytes it wrote. The kernel has a body on x86-64 alone, so the catch is the script,
  which builds the binary for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64, whose
  max model has AVX2 on every host. The lane skips without docker, and
  this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    COMPRESS_BLOCKS(h, p, blocks);
    wipe_frame_call();
--- new
    COMPRESS_BLOCKS(h, p, blocks);
#ifdef CH_SHA512_AVX2_COPY
    (void)wipe_frame_call;
#else
    wipe_frame_call();
#endif
